                <pb facs="0225" n="191" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg191"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr.
                            Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-12-03"><hi rendition="#italic">December 3, 1897</hi></date>.
                        (Received December 18.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 207.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your instruction No. 227, of
                    November 20, containing a report upon the cases of trichinae in German pork,
                    based upon a careful investigation made by the Secretary of Agriculture, I beg
                    to say that the interesting and valuable data contained therein will be
                    transmitted immediately to the Imperial foreign office.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">And. D. White.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
